            <ArticleTitle>Aortic subannular left ventricular aneurysm: a rare and surgically correctable cause of angina.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>313-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.athoracsur.2013.04.130</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0003-4975(13)01127-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aortic subannular left ventricular aneurysm is a rare form of cardiac pathology. We report a case, including noninvasive and intraoperative imaging, of this entity in a young woman presenting with angina. The patient underwent successful surgical repair and is now asymptomatic.</AbstractText>
